{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfdDLf2BiXGPiaERUF2jF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the answer now.\n\nTo make the pipeline wait, write a `Blocked-by: #41` line on its own line in issue 42's body or any comment on its thread (cross-repo works too, as `Blocked-by: owner/repo#41`). `scripts/gather-issues.sh` checks that reference live and drops issue 42 as a candidate for as long as #41 stays open — this is a deterministic, code-enforced dependency gate (requirement 34j in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-PIPELINE-SPEC.md`), not a judgement call a model has to re-derive from prose each cycle.\n\nYou won't need to remember to undo it: once #41 is merged/closed, the same mechanism re-checks the reference live and releases the hold automatically — there's nothing to edit out, and a stale `Blocked-by:` line naming an already-closed issue is simply inert, never re-triggering a block. The one thing *not* to use for this is a prose note like \"hold until #41 is merged\" — the spec explicitly flags that pattern as the thing this convention replaces, because a model re-reading such a note can re-block the issue even after the dependency has actually resolved.\n\nSources: docs/IMPLEMENTATION-PIPELINE-SPEC.md, requirement 34j (\"A structured dependency is held, and released, by code — never by a model re-reading prose\")."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":34863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2517},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e74a7a7b-2d45-42ed-87f9-849aebbe1d13","uuid":"b407a47a-fed9-47bd-964a-f2c70794c270","timestamp":"2026-10-02T09:58:39.341Z","request_id":"req_011CfdDLegqVtko3pCCA53zY"}
